SUMMARY:Josh Johnson's Comedy Band Camp LIVE at Palace Theatre Columbus (Ea
	rly Show)
DTSTAMP:20260731T111853Z
DTSTART:20260731T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official Tickets\nResale Tickets\n\nAbout Josh Johnson\nJosh Jo
	hnson is one of the most exciting comedians in the game right now. With ov
	er 10 million followers across social media\, WIRED called him “the funnie
	st guy on the internet.” He is an Emmy-nominated writer\, stand-up comedia
	n\, actor\, and NAACP award-winner from Louisiana by way of Chicago. \nJoh
	nson is currently a rotating host and correspondent on Comedy Central’s Em
	my and Peabody Award-winning program The Daily Show. He is also a prolific
	 creator who puts out weekly stand-up sets on his YouTube channel — conten
	t that has been viewed over half a billion times worldwide. In 2025\, he r
	eleased an astonishing 38 hours of topical stand-up material performed in 
	front of live audiences. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Friday\, July 31\, 2026\
	nTime: 7:00 PM (Early Show)\nVenue: Palace Theatre Columbus\nAddress: 34 W
	. Broad St.\, Columbus\, OH 43215\nTicket Price Range: Starting at $91+\nN
	ote: Two shows available this night — 7:00 PM (Early) and 10:00 PM (Late)\
	n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Palace Theatre Columbus is a magnificent historic 
	venue located at 34 W. Broad St. in the heart of downtown Columbus. Built 
	in 1926\, this stunning theater is one of the most beautiful performance s
	paces in Ohio\, featuring ornate architecture\, a grand lobby\, and except
	ional acoustics. \nOperated by CAPA (Columbus Association for the Performi
	ng Arts)\, the Palace Theatre seats approximately 2\,800 guests and offers
	 a truly special atmosphere for live entertainment. The venue’s classic de
	sign creates an intimate feel despite its size\, with excellent sightlines
	 from all seating areas. The Palace is easily accessible from throughout C
	olumbus and is surrounded by downtown dining and entertainment options. \n
	Parking is available in several nearby garages and surface lots in downtow
	n Columbus. The venue is also accessible via COTA bus routes. Arrive early
	 to take in the stunning architecture and grab a drink before the show. \n
	What to Expect\nJosh Johnson’s Comedy Band Camp is a unique and innovative
	 comedy experience that goes beyond a traditional stand-up show. The show 
	features Josh’s signature topical humor\, sharp social commentary\, and th
	e kind of intelligent\, thought-provoking comedy that has made him one of 
	the most talked-about performers of his generation. \nThe show incorporate
	s musical elements and a full cast of performers\, creating an immersive e
	ntertainment experience unlike anything else on tour. Fans who have follow
	ed Josh on The Daily Show or his YouTube channel will recognize his abilit
	y to make sense of the world through humor — but seeing it live takes the 
	experience to a whole new level. \nWith two shows on the same night\, the 
	early show at 7:00 PM is perfect for those who want to be home at a reason
	able hour. Doors typically open 30-60 minutes before showtime. \nTicket In
	formation\nTickets start at $91 and are available through CAPA/Ticketmaste
	r and VividSeats. Josh Johnson shows have been selling out across the coun
	try — grab your tickets now! \n\nOfficial Tickets\nResale Tickets\n\nThis 
	post contains affiliate links. We earn a commission if you purchase ticket
	s through our links at no extra cost to you. \nAll sales are final. Show t
	imes subject to change. Valid photo ID may be required for entry.\n\nhttps
	://comedycalendar.com/event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at-palace-
	theatre-columbus-early-show/\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at
	-palace-theatre-columbus-early-show/
LOCATION:Palace Theatre Columbus\, 34 W. Broad St.\, Columbus\, OH\, 43215\
	, United States Of America
